# eirl-storage-format@<seq>: `eirl-storage format <seq>` in the system's mount namespace (RECORDING.md §4), like
# eirl-storage-eject.service: the app runs `sudo eirl-storage format` with the seq of the disk the user confirmed on
# stdin, which starts this unit and returns its exit status. It formats only if the state's seq is still that one. It ends by restarting eirl-storage@<disk>.service, which mounts the new filesystem: the exFAT FUSE daemon must
# live in that unit, not in this one, whose processes systemd kills when it finishes. Not enabled.
[Unit]
Description=eirl-storage: format the USB disk of local recordings as exFAT
Documentation=https://github.com/enhanced-irl/eirl-encoder/blob/main/RECORDING.md

[Service]
Type=oneshot
Environment=EIRL_STORAGE_DIRECT=1
ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/eirl-storage format %i
# Partitioning and mkfs.exfat, then the disk's unit restarted (its own limit is 10 minutes)
TimeoutStartSec=1200
